            <ArticleTitle>Right coronary artery originating from distal left circumflex: an unusual feature of single coronary artery.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>746-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This report describes a patient with a single coronary artery system, in whom the right coronary artery originated from the distal left circumflex. A significant stenosis was present just at the take-off of the aberrant right coronary artery. No other associated cardiac anomaly could be demonstrated; the patient was referred for elective bypass surgery.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
